the realm  do you know what the realm is  it's the thousand blades of aegon's  enemies  a story we agreed to tell each other  over  and over till we forget that it's a lie  what's up ladies and gentlemen welcome  back for another game of thrones season  8 video in this video i want to do  something a little different i want to  give my thoughts about why i think the  night king was afraid to fight jon snow  during the long night battle at  winterfell at first this answer might  seem kinda obvious when you think about  it however in order for this to actually  work we will have to go back a few  seasons when we all thought everything  in game of thrones had some sort of  meaning to it now we all remember how  game of thrones ended at least for some  of us it kind of seemed like a lot of  things were meaningless in the end  however it wasn't always like this back  when i first started making game of  thrones videos around season 6 and  season 7 it seemed like every single  scene had some sort of significance and  in one way or another it would have an  effect on the ending i don't know about  all of you but this was when the game of  thrones fandom was the most fun  my absolute favorite thing about game of  thrones was all the different theories  surrounding it back then it honestly  seemed like there was an endless amount  of ways this show could have actually  ended unfortunately as we all know a lot  of those ideas fizzled out by the final  season once we saw the direction the  game of thrones writers david and dan  were heading in  now even with that in mind i still want  to do something a little different with  this video like i said at the beginning  if we go back only a few seasons when we  all thought every scene in game of  thrones had meaning i think we might be  able to see why the night king was  afraid to fight jon snow in the end but  like i said this idea will only work if  we look at the show through that lens i  think the reason why the night king did  not want to fight jon snow one versus  one was because of what he saw john do  back at heart home now if you remember  when jon snow defeated his first white  walker the night king was actually  watching jon when that happened not only  was the night king watching but judging  by the look on his face it seemed like  he knew there was something very special  about jon snow or at the very least he  knew there was something very special  about jon snow's sword then when the  night king finally saw jon snow again  during the long night battle for  winterfell he did not forget what he saw  him do back at heart home  so maybe just maybe he knew jon snow  would do the same exact thing to him if  he engaged him in a one versus one sword  fight this and honestly only this is the  only way i can justify the night king  not wanting to fight jon snow in the end  i mean let's be honest it would have  been really stupid for the night king to  fight jon if he knew he was vulnerable  to valyrian steel like the other white  walkers were not only would this explain  why the night king avoided fighting him  but it would also give more significance  to the scene when the night king was  looking on as jon snow defeated the  white walker at harthome again we all  know most of the foreshadowing went  right out of the window like brain stark  by the final season but i think this  does make some sense of that scene let  me know what all of you think down below  does this work for you or do you still  think that scene made no sense  whatsoever believe me i will not be mad  if you think it was dumb no one was more  upset than i was when the night king  died before fighting jon snow and if you  know you know this isn't even the most  upsetting thing about this what makes  jon snow not fighting the night king  even worse is the fact that the actor  who was the night king is arguably one  of the most badass fight choreographers  in all of hollywood the man has been  showing actors most notably he showed  all the game of thrones actors how to  fight with a sword he had been doing  this for over 30 years as a matter of  fact he was the stand-in for all the sir  arthur dane fight scenes now the actor  who was standing right here acting like  he was sir arthur dain was not the same  man who did the sword fighting once his  helmet hit his face the man who was  fighting with a sword in each hand was  the same guy who was the night king so  just imagine how amazing the fight  scenes could have been if only jon snow  was allowed to fight the night king  before the show ended i mean how can you  give the night king this awesome magical  ice sword and have a 30-year veteran  stunt coordinator as the night king yet  not let him use that in the final season  during the biggest battle we had all  been waiting for since literally the  opening scene of the opening episode now  i could go on and on about this for days  but i won't do that because it will only  make me even more upset when i think  about it the only way i can stop myself  from being mad about this is if i give  these scenes some sort of meaning by  telling myself the night king was too  afraid to fight jon snow because of what  he saw at heart home then again maybe  i'm just making excuses  as always let me know what all of you  think leave your thoughts down below i  will be reading them once this video  goes live  i want to thank all of you once again  for watching my videos i hope everyone  has a great day i will see you soon in  the next one bye  so  [Music]  you

